{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47716-conspiracy-theory-truths-valkyrie","id":47716,"title":"Conspiracy Theory Truths & VALKYRIE","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-12T17:07:22-08:00","id":47716,"title":"Conspiracy Theory Truths & VALKYRIE","content":"So the VALKYRIE write-up makes reference to high ranked agents knowing things like &quot;who really shot Kennedy&quot;. I'm curious what some thoughts are on these possibilities for the WoD. Remember, the point of Tier 3 is to play around in the gonzo world-shaping conspiracy stuff ala the CWoD.<br /> <br /> Kennedy Assassination Possibilities<br /> - the Warren Report is 100% correct, but ADAMSKI is using the assassination as a decoy from other events/efforts<br /> <br /> - As above, except ADAMSKI as Oswald killed to facilitate it. Or perhaps because Oswald was going to be railing too much about how &quot;the Machine told me to do it&quot;...<br /> <br /> - Witches were carrying out a ritual, intentionally orchestrating the Lincoln-Kennedy coincidences. They'd attempted this before using the Garfield and McKinnley assassinations and the physical presence of Robert Todd Lincoln to ritually tie the events together. After that was foiled a fourth time, and Robert passed away, they turned to other means to complete the ritual. Oswald was controlled by a Profane Urim. His puppeteer was on the grassy knoll. Whether the ritual succeded or not is a bit ambiguous (it's possible it didn't because the truth of the Lincoln assassination wasn't known to cabal of government-infiltrating witches in question). In any event, VALKYRIE spent the next decade hunting them down.<br /> <br /> - JFK had become compromised by supernatural influences (perhaps he had turned to vampire blood or a Demon Pact to treat his Addison's disease) and VALKYRIE took him out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Possibly simply because I'm not British I have no decent conspiracy on the Diana secret mentioned in the Hunter core. This Mitchell and Webb sketch I think addresses why: <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b4meFC1ee7Q\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b4meFC1ee7Q</a><br /> <br /> The one idea I do have is that the Incarnae Diana (see Shadows of the UK) was coming into existence without a defined form yet before she died, and that ENE is what VALKYRIE is aware as &quot;who else was in the car&quot;, as it rose out of the ashes with its now defined nature.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So obviously in the NWoD, the Moon Landing happened (its how Idigam got back to Earth), but my thinking is that VALKYRIE censored the footage and what actually happened there, and what was found. That's the reason for the sound gap between &quot;One small step for&quot; and &quot;man&quot; (it was meant to be &quot;A man&quot;; and Armstrong's sure that's what he said).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T12:21:04-08:00","id":48390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47716-conspiracy-theory-truths-valkyrie#post47716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the VALKYRIE write-up makes reference to high ranked agents knowing things like &quot;who really shot Kennedy&quot;. I'm curious what some thoughts are on these possibilities for the WoD. Remember, the point of Tier 3 is to play around in the gonzo world-shaping conspiracy stuff ala the CWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd actually disagree that Tier 3 is world changing or gonzo.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that most of the Conspiracies have realatively low key goals: TF:V - protect america, VASCU - arrest serial killers, Cheiron - make lots of money, Lucifuge - keep the devil's children too busy to do evil, MM - kill vampires, witches and demons.<br /> <br /> You don't see that much about trying to take over the world, becoming Gods or conquering countries. It's there, like Lucifuge's Reconciliation or the AKD's secret goal, but mostly Tier 3 means you have more resources to accomplish the same sorts of goals that the previous tiers did. Killing monsters.<br /> <br /> <br /> So that said, my suggestion for the Kennady assassination is to pick a real conspiracy theory (or list several) with no supernatural involvement. TF:V just knows about it because TF:V knows about most things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/47716-conspiracy-theory-truths-valkyrie#post47716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly simply because I'm not British I have no decent conspiracy on the Diana secret mentioned in the Hunter core. This Mitchell and Webb sketch I think addresses why: <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b4meFC1ee7Q\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b4meFC1ee7Q</a><br /> <br /> The one idea I do have is that the Incarnae Diana (see Shadows of the UK) was coming into existence without a defined form yet before she died, and that ENE is what VALKYRIE is aware as &quot;who else was in the car&quot;, as it rose out of the ashes with its now defined nature.</div> </div> </div> </div> Saying it's the Incarnae is a nifty solution; Mitchell and Webb were completely right (and hilarious about it) to say that there's probably no conspiracy at all and not much mileage in imagining one. I would probably say it's closet to a &quot;premonition&quot; or something of the Incarnae.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Just as an aside, I wouldn't use Shadows of the UK too much. I'm not saying it's a bad book, it's a good one even if it's not to my tastes, but it's a bit outdated in it's idea of what a British WoD game should look like. How to put it...<br /> <br /> Ok, the nWoD always sat somewhere between Horror and Urban Fantasy. It's got urban fantasy calling cards like vampire politics, but also focuses a lot on why it's horrific to be supernatural (to a greater or lesser extent in different gamelines).<br /> <br /> British horror focuses (or at least it did when Shadows of the UK was written, I'm not a pure horror fan and am going by SotUK's opening to chapter 3) on dis-empowerment and fatalism. Personally I would say that's more horrific than horror that focuses on a dangerous monster. Meanwhile the biggest influence on recent British Urban Fantasy is probably Doctor Who, seriously - Ben Aaaronovitch, Toby Whithouse, Paul Cournel, Neil Gaiman, all worked on Doctor Who. Kate Griffin is a lifelong fan but never worked on it and except for Neil they all did Doctor Who before their famous Urban Fantasy work.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that British Urban Fantasy is light hearted, child-friendly fun like Doctor Who. Being Human got really dark at times (and almost completely deconstructed angsty vampires, it was <b>awesome</b> in series 1-3. I'm still sad they left one small thread of deconstruction untied), so does the brilliant London Falling (a must read for Hunter fans). Rather I'm saying that no matter how dark they get there's often an element of Doctor Who like quirkiness, humour and a love of finding wonder in the mundane (one thing I've noticed, muggles - and I'm calling Hunters nonMuggle - and their institutions usually get more plot agency in British works).<br /> <br /> <br /> So that leads to an interesting conundrum. The WoD always was a blend of both horror and urban fantasy; however SotUK reccomends a grim fatalistic mood for UK horror, while even the darkest UK urban fantasy has a quirky mundanity to it. Blending them won't work.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that SotUK was wrong to resolve this conundrum by going full horror - even though I prefer Urban Fantasy myself - but I am saying that it's outdated because it pre-dates this issue and thus neglects to address it. Though how they didn't create an Incarnae for the NHS just boggles the mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> Coincidently if you ever wondered why the Lord Stewards break quite a few unwritten Hunter assumptions, it's because they're quite intentionally based on British Urban Fantasy conventions rather than American ones.<br /> <br /> <br /> =======================<br /> <br /> So back to topic. More Conspiracy theories and how they fit into the WoD.<br /> <br /> The royal family aren't space lizards, but they have some dragon blood in them from the White Dragon of the Anglo Saxons*. Though only as magical as the average Wolf-Blood, dragons blood is pretty useful in magic ceremonies. Especially those that connect the crown to the land. (Yep, Elizabeth II is a direct heir to the Anglo Saxon kings, William the Conqueror's youngest son married an Anglo Saxon Princess and their grandson became king)<br /> <br /> * That would probably imply the same of most Europeans monarchs and a good chunk of the population then. You could avoid that by saying it only lasts in the British royalty for mystical reasons.<br /> <br /> <br /> Roswell: That &quot;weather balloon&quot; actually was a weather balloon. TF:V knew that Faerie Tokens always had a Catch and a Drawback, so they decided that the early test should be highly deniable. When it naturally went wrong they chucked the token back into storage and left the rest of the weather balloon back into storage. A few Alien like True Fae were attracted by stories centered unknowingly around a Token, and now primarally abduct from the Roswell area.<br /> <br /> <br /> In contrast the Bermuda Triangle was targeted by actual space aliens. TF:V suspects they went there because it's such a popular shipping route. When TF:V tried to investigate they just flew off and no one's seen them around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-13-2014, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T13:26:23-08:00","id":48436,"title":"","content":"Mage gives a story to both the Templar theories and the Merovingians/Priory of scion theories.<br /> <br /> For the JFK assassination I'd be tempted to make it the result of a supernatural being, but for extremely mundane reasons; all you'd need is one aggrieved Cuban Masitgos. I just like the idea of playing with expectations, the truth is just as boring as the Lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T21:07:22-08:00","id":48702,"title":"","content":"The US government's efforts to dose the public with various diseases during the Cold War wasn't just to test dispersion patterns and rates of infection. Cheiron was desperate to get government funding for black budget work on viral warfare, so with the proper donations to the right coffers the DOD decided to make the tests a reality. It got a giant shot in the arm after it was revealed the Soviet government <i>was</i> planning such attacks on American waterways.<br /> <br /> TWA 800? Someone on that plane had information very damaging to certain concerns in Milan. Whether it was a defector to another conspiracy, or an outside party thinking it had uncovered something Earth shattering, it didn't matter when something tore apart the plane from the inside and lit the fuel tanks.<br /> <br /> The &quot;October Surprise&quot;, the release of the American hostages from Iran? The Ascending Ones. Reagan winning the election would have only strengthened the war on drugs, a move which would make the drug trade even more profitable for those that knew exactly how to funnel it into the country and sell it best. Prices go up, but production costs still stay the same overseas. More money for the vigil. They're also the reason why programs like DARE are so ineffective; the more you tell some people <i>not</i> to do something...<br /> <br /> The Vela Incident is the second-to-greatest screw-up on the part of the Knights of St. George. The double-flash was actually part of a ritual that nearly drew the attention of another faceless angel to the world. Covered as a South African nuclear test, the second flash was the failsafe to prevent anything from entering into our world should the ritual go wrong. The fact that it went off a split-second after the first should tell people all they need to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}